  "findings": [
    "All stored seconds equal raw EXPLAIN Execution Time in milliseconds divided by 1000; no unit conversion error found.",
    "Warm plans use index-only scans; root Shared Read Blocks is zero for all six cases. This is PostgreSQL-buffer evidence, not a claim about host-wide I/O.",
    "q05 returns 44,118,358 neighbors; incoming branches return 0,0,6. The seeds provide narrow incoming-citation coverage.",
    "q06 is one-seed outgoing-outgoing count DISTINCT, not global graph analytics; joined pairs are 920,848,4230.",
    "Warm largest-seed q06 execution median2.708ms vs primer437.932ms. Primer is not a controlled cold-cache experiment.",
    "EXPLAIN omits planning and actual result delivery. The reported server medians are not network-inclusive request times.",
    "client_seconds is not clean request latency: timer includes Monitor.start/stop and sampling plus plan transfer; these windows are around23\u201327ms for warm graph cases.",
    "qa.fetch_seconds is one later same-host SELECT/fetch/canonicalization observation, not three warm latency repeats or a remote-client benchmark.",
    "The reported family ratios compare maximum seed medians independently; the q06 maxima come from different seeds. Same-seed q06 ratios differ.",
    "Keep server timings unchanged; retract broad 1300x/150x application-speed interpretation. Request-level speedup is unmeasured."
